(4510497, 648945, 68035, '<td valign="top">I had to pause on this shot for a moment in that my initial reactions were ''sensationist rubbish'' and ''yep peace at last except for the family are left behind when things like this happen'' and I was going for the 3 button.  Then I realised that any image that can cause the viewer to feel emotion (be they positive or negative) can perhaps be classified as a good image.  So tried to view it a little more subjectively.  In the end I gave it a six as I feel that the shot did not quite convey any real sense of peace even in death and also the focus on the face seems slightly off.<br/> <br/>Not a shot I remotely like but hopefully one that has let me overcome my prejudices and mark fairly</td>', 'I had to pause on this shot for a moment in that my initial reactions were ''sensationist rubbish'' and ''yep peace at last except for the family are left behind when things like this happen'' and I was going for the 3 button.  Then I realised that any image that can cause the viewer to feel emotion (be they positive or negative) can perhaps be classified as a good image.  So tried to view it a little more subjectively.  In the end I gave it a six as I feel that the shot did not quite convey any real sense of peace even in death and also the focus on the face seems slightly off. Not a shot I remotely like but hopefully one that has let me overcome my prejudices and mark fairly', '2008-02-23 17:29:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(4510499, 647152, 68035, '<td valign="top">Almost but not quite a great image.  The dimensions are a little offputting and there seems to be quite a bit of noise (especially where the cloud filters into the skyline) still a nice image 6</td>', 'Almost but not quite a great image.  The dimensions are a little offputting and there seems to be quite a bit of noise (especially where the cloud filters into the skyline) still a nice image 6', '2008-02-23 17:31:19.000000', NULL, 1),
