(4520088, 647943, 42495, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Arcanist:</b></div><hr/><i> You should calibrate your monitor soon.  While the image entered is viewable, it is only noticable on a calibrated monitor if we adjust the gamma and backlighting to the positive scale by a lot.  (Your monitor is too bright to be editing pics on.) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I calibrated mine last night and it looks just fine without adjusting gamma and backlighting.</td>', 'Originally posted by Arcanist: You should calibrate your monitor soon.  While the image entered is viewable, it is only noticable on a calibrated monitor if we adjust the gamma and backlighting to the positive scale by a lot.  (Your monitor is too bright to be editing pics on.)   I calibrated mine last night and it looks just fine without adjusting gamma and backlighting.', '2008-02-27 01:01:48.000000', NULL, 0),
