(4525940, 648961, 70128, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by photon:</b></div><hr/><i> looks like bogas voting going on. why would anyone vote this a 2 or 3 ?<br/>Or a 4 or 5 for that matter !!! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I agree... I always wonder what do DPCers think of when voting... or is it that they want to win and rate low to take advantage? I don''t get it... besides they don''t leave comments when rating low... this photograph is excellent!</td>', 'Originally posted by photon: looks like bogas voting going on. why would anyone vote this a 2 or 3 ?Or a 4 or 5 for that matter !!!   I agree... I always wonder what do DPCers think of when voting... or is it that they want to win and rate low to take advantage? I don''t get it... besides they don''t leave comments when rating low... this photograph is excellent!', '2008-02-28 17:54:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4526960, 648710, 30982, '<td valign="top">I think in a lot of cases people do not look beyond their own little worlds, which is quite sad.  This is an exceptional take on the challenge and an enjoyable photograph to view.</td>', 'I think in a lot of cases people do not look beyond their own little worlds, which is quite sad.  This is an exceptional take on the challenge and an enjoyable photograph to view.', '2008-02-29 03:38:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(4526961, 648957, 30982, '<td valign="top">LOL!!  Peas are best eaten raw, by the way.  Preferably right after you pull the pod off the vine.  Then they are crunchy and sweet and absolutely wonderful.</td>', 'LOL!!  Peas are best eaten raw, by the way.  Preferably right after you pull the pod off the vine.  Then they are crunchy and sweet and absolutely wonderful.', '2008-02-29 03:40:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(4526963, 647943, 30982, '<td valign="top">I can see this just fine on my work monitor - I suspect on my home monitor I might have trouble with it.  The concept is excellent - a baby peacefully sleeping in the dark - and would NOT work as well if it were more strongly lit.  The problem with the internet is everyone''s monitors will vary.  This is one of those shots that will have a lot more impact printed, when everyone can view it the same.  I really like your choice to enter this, though I sympathize with your score.</td>', 'I can see this just fine on my work monitor - I suspect on my home monitor I might have trouble with it.  The concept is excellent - a baby peacefully sleeping in the dark - and would NOT work as well if it were more strongly lit.  The problem with the internet is everyone''s monitors will vary.  This is one of those shots that will have a lot more impact printed, when everyone can view it the same.  I really like your choice to enter this, though I sympathize with your score.', '2008-02-29 03:45:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(4526978, 647210, 37252, '<td valign="top">This is an excellent capture! Perfect DOF and focus on details. The composition is very pleasing. Congrats on a well deserved ribbon.</td>', 'This is an excellent capture! Perfect DOF and focus on details. The composition is very pleasing. Congrats on a well deserved ribbon.', '2008-02-29 04:25:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4527239, 648940, 77196, '<td valign="top">Beautifully done. The dark background makes the bright yellow bills and white stand out nicely. <br/> <br/>After trying to photograph birds on the water, I have a new appreciation for just how hard it is to do well, and this is beyond well, well into excellent.</td>', 'Beautifully done. The dark background makes the bright yellow bills and white stand out nicely.  After trying to photograph birds on the water, I have a new appreciation for just how hard it is to do well, and this is beyond well, well into excellent.', '2008-02-29 07:26:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(4527479, 649044, 50641, '<td valign="top">Love the idea and admire your devil-may-care in entering it.</td>', 'Love the idea and admire your devil-may-care in entering it.', '2008-02-29 09:29:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(4527917, 646893, 44877, '<td valign="top">This is absolutely stunning. I didn''t vote on the Peace challenge and didn''t even see most of it. Hadn''t you gotten the Posthumous blue, I would have missed it altogether. <br/> <br/>Well seen and most superbly processed.<br/> <br/>Edit to add: I was just reading some of the comments about cutting out the cord. <br/> <br/>Don''t cut out the cord! It makes the shot - I am baffled by the ignorance of people suggesting you should change the composition of this photo - don''t listen to them.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-02-29 12:00:41.</i></td>', 'This is absolutely stunning. I didn''t vote on the Peace challenge and didn''t even see most of it. Hadn''t you gotten the Posthumous blue, I would have missed it altogether.  Well seen and most superbly processed. Edit to add: I was just reading some of the comments about cutting out the cord.  Don''t cut out the cord! It makes the shot - I am baffled by the ignorance of people suggesting you should change the composition of this photo - don''t listen to them.', '2008-02-29 11:57:31.000000', '2008-02-29 12:00:41.000000', 0),
(4527967, 646893, 7778, '<td valign="top">This is one hell of a shot/model/posture/composition/manner. The impromptu litter and cabling in the foreground adds some surreality to the glamour. The Chaucerian spelling of ''soule'' doesn''t do any harm either.The classic manner, however, appears somewhat impaired by over-sharpening, at least to my trained eye. :-)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-02-29 12:26:36.</i></td>', 'This is one hell of a shot/model/posture/composition/manner. The impromptu litter and cabling in the foreground adds some surreality to the glamour. The Chaucerian spelling of ''soule'' doesn''t do any harm either.The classic manner, however, appears somewhat impaired by over-sharpening, at least to my trained eye. :-)', '2008-02-29 12:24:50.000000', '2008-02-29 12:26:36.000000', 0),
(4528910, 648961, 73980, '<td valign="top">Beautiful colors and light!  Congrats on the ribbon.</td>', 'Beautiful colors and light!  Congrats on the ribbon.', '2008-02-29 23:08:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(4529418, 648605, 62357, '<td valign="top">This is lovely Sara.</td>', 'This is lovely Sara.', '2008-03-01 02:34:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(4530492, 648940, 88924, '<td valign="top">congrats. it''s a beautiful image. great use of negative space and lovely tones.</td>', 'congrats. it''s a beautiful image. great use of negative space and lovely tones.', '2008-03-01 13:11:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4532510, 648957, 68035, '<td valign="top">Well casting aside for a moment your dislike of peas (surely your ire would be better focused on natures real sins...broccoli and sprouts)<br/> <br/>The shot and the title did both make me smile.  I was slightly put off by the water underneath the peas (where they frozen and had just started to melt?).  Nice complementary colours and I liked the dof you used</td>', 'Well casting aside for a moment your dislike of peas (surely your ire would be better focused on natures real sins...broccoli and sprouts) The shot and the title did both make me smile.  I was slightly put off by the water underneath the peas (where they frozen and had just started to melt?).  Nice complementary colours and I liked the dof you used', '2008-03-02 12:16:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(4532528, 648978, 68035, '<td valign="top">There is a wonderful sense of tranquility in this shot.  I liked the centred but at a slight angle composition<br/> <br/>Very nice portrait for which I think the high key black and white works well</td>', 'There is a wonderful sense of tranquility in this shot.  I liked the centred but at a slight angle composition Very nice portrait for which I think the high key black and white works well', '2008-03-02 12:24:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(4532571, 648871, 33732, '<td valign="top">I really like this.  Moving water is nice.</td>', 'I really like this.  Moving water is nice.', '2008-03-02 12:46:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(4532609, 648746, 33732, '<td valign="top">Where was the location?  I like it.</td>', 'Where was the location?  I like it.', '2008-03-02 13:18:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(4533094, 648839, 85102, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Sammie:</b></div><hr/><i> This is nice. Was it hard to draw the peace sign and not leave footprints in the sand? The whole scene is very peaceful, too - it was a good place to draw a peace sign! </i></td></tr></table> <br/>haha yea, a little bit, i had a bunch of outtakes with my foot prints all over the place!</td>', 'Originally posted by Sammie: This is nice. Was it hard to draw the peace sign and not leave footprints in the sand? The whole scene is very peaceful, too - it was a good place to draw a peace sign!  haha yea, a little bit, i had a bunch of outtakes with my foot prints all over the place!', '2008-03-02 18:05:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(4534987, 648957, 52115, '<td valign="top">Nice composition, the peas look too, real not shiny and spotless like on the label. The peas need more makeup, or shot in the raw.</td>', 'Nice composition, the peas look too, real not shiny and spotless like on the label. The peas need more makeup, or shot in the raw.', '2008-03-03 10:56:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4536547, 647210, 90990, '<td valign="top">Fantastic capture!!!<br/> <br/>Regards,<br/>D</td>', 'Fantastic capture!!! Regards,D', '2008-03-03 21:55:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(4537203, 648940, 81952, '<td valign="top">getting peace takes effort it prooves :D</td>', 'getting peace takes effort it prooves :D', '2008-03-04 08:56:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(4537494, 647152, 51538, '<td valign="top">I think this photo is glorious.  It''s like an advert for the new age that is coming upon us.  I just wish Sara was in there too.  In my opinion, the grain/noise really enhances the image.  Most people go for a very smooth effect in processing sunsets.  I guess they feel that smooth, tranquil, and hypnotizing the viewer all go together.  The impressionist painters did not do smooth though and they were very successful.</td>', 'I think this photo is glorious.  It''s like an advert for the new age that is coming upon us.  I just wish Sara was in there too.  In my opinion, the grain/noise really enhances the image.  Most people go for a very smooth effect in processing sunsets.  I guess they feel that smooth, tranquil, and hypnotizing the viewer all go together.  The impressionist painters did not do smooth though and they were very successful.', '2008-03-04 12:04:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(4538042, 647210, 87097, '<td valign="top">Whoever rating this 5 or below is delusional. Fantastic capture of an undoubtedly rare moment!</td>', 'Whoever rating this 5 or below is delusional. Fantastic capture of an undoubtedly rare moment!', '2008-03-04 16:22:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4542749, 648864, 88656, '<td valign="top">I am sorry you got landed on, but i hope it was worth it cause this is a cool picture!</td>', 'I am sorry you got landed on, but i hope it was worth it cause this is a cool picture!', '2008-03-06 09:09:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4543611, 648710, 62318, '<td valign="top">No matter the challenge topic, I have always a big fan of these types of shots (though this fits in my opinion). Real shots with real emotions. Terrific.</td>', 'No matter the challenge topic, I have always a big fan of these types of shots (though this fits in my opinion). Real shots with real emotions. Terrific.', '2008-03-06 15:14:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(4544319, 646830, 47852, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by vlado:</b></div><hr/><i> Good photo... the finger/other hand is extremely distracting though... would have been one of the best of these types of photos in this challenge (and there were a few) if not for that finger/other hand  :( </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>As a kindergarten teacher, I used to use a hand signal like this to get the kids quieted down... a "shhh" over the lips and two "bunny ears" on the other hand to show they were ready to listen.  So I don''t find the other hand distracting at all, in fact I find it to be a nice depiction of what a kid might think of as peace and quiet.<br/> <br/>If I find anything in the shot distracting, it would have to be that upper left corner in the background.  I don''t know what it is, but I find myself looking at it and wondering, which detracts my attention from the main focus.  I do think the shot is a bit flat though.. perhaps a boost in the contrast to make the whites more white and the blacks more black would help this shot.</td>', 'Originally posted by vlado: Good photo... the finger/other hand is extremely distracting though... would have been one of the best of these types of photos in this challenge (and there were a few) if not for that finger/other hand  :(   As a kindergarten teacher, I used to use a hand signal like this to get the kids quieted down... a "shhh" over the lips and two "bunny ears" on the other hand to show they were ready to listen.  So I don''t find the other hand distracting at all, in fact I find it to be a nice depiction of what a kid might think of as peace and quiet. If I find anything in the shot distracting, it would have to be that upper left corner in the background.  I don''t know what it is, but I find myself looking at it and wondering, which detracts my attention from the main focus.  I do think the shot is a bit flat though.. perhaps a boost in the contrast to make the whites more white and the blacks more black would help this shot.', '2008-03-06 21:56:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(4544464, 648882, 89906, '<td valign="top">She Is beautiful.<br/>:)</td>', 'She Is beautiful.:)', '2008-03-07 00:00:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(4544558, 649048, 91118, '<td valign="top">In spite of the things you stated you could have done better, i am abolutely in love with this picture. The contrast is so neat. i love it.</td>', 'In spite of the things you stated you could have done better, i am abolutely in love with this picture. The contrast is so neat. i love it.', '2008-03-07 01:52:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(4544710, 646830, 67258, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 7, and thought it one of the stronger images in the challenge.  I love the appearance of sponteneity; I realise from your notes that this is an illusion, but that is pretty much what all photography is!  Your depth of field is absolutely spot on, as is the lighting.  the tonal range of your mono conversion is good, although there aren''t any whites to provide contrast.  With regards to your young model - you''ve got a good one there, I''d keep him ;-).  The chipped and slightly mucky finger nails are a nice touch, and add to the emotive, story-telling aspect.  I am with kteach in thatthe change i light in the upper left is slightly distracting - it was the thing thta prevented me from bumping you to an 8.  <br/> <br/>A word of warning about the scores at DPC - don''t take the end score as a measure of a photos value.  To me the value of a photo is in the impact, particlarly lasting impact, that a photo has on a single viewer.  This is one that I enjoyed viewing, and look forward to coming across again.  It is a photo that I want to explore, not just with my eyes but with my brain too, if that makes any sense?</td>', 'I gave this a 7, and thought it one of the stronger images in the challenge.  I love the appearance of sponteneity; I realise from your notes that this is an illusion, but that is pretty much what all photography is!  Your depth of field is absolutely spot on, as is the lighting.  the tonal range of your mono conversion is good, although there aren''t any whites to provide contrast.  With regards to your young model - you''ve got a good one there, I''d keep him ;-).  The chipped and slightly mucky finger nails are a nice touch, and add to the emotive, story-telling aspect.  I am with kteach in thatthe change i light in the upper left is slightly distracting - it was the thing thta prevented me from bumping you to an 8.   A word of warning about the scores at DPC - don''t take the end score as a measure of a photos value.  To me the value of a photo is in the impact, particlarly lasting impact, that a photo has on a single viewer.  This is one that I enjoyed viewing, and look forward to coming across again.  It is a photo that I want to explore, not just with my eyes but with my brain too, if that makes any sense?', '2008-03-07 05:46:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(4545280, 646637, 30861, '<td valign="top">This is hauntingly reminiscent of my "self portrait as raindrop" in concept and execution. I''m surprised I didn''t notice it before. I don''t mean "you copied me", I mean "you took an eerily similar approach", like we are thinking the same way, far outside the box. So I''m glad I''m not the only one. Fore reference, if you don''t know that image (it was 4 years ago), here it is:<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=146162" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/308/120/146162.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/308/120/146162.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/0-999/308/120/146162.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>Check out the photographer''s comments, and the back-and-forth in the comments thread. People have a REALLY hard time "getting" this stuff. But I "get" it and I love it.</td>', 'This is hauntingly reminiscent of my "self portrait as raindrop" in concept and execution. I''m surprised I didn''t notice it before. I don''t mean "you copied me", I mean "you took an eerily similar approach", like we are thinking the same way, far outside the box. So I''m glad I''m not the only one. Fore reference, if you don''t know that image (it was 4 years ago), here it is:   Check out the photographer''s comments, and the back-and-forth in the comments thread. People have a REALLY hard time "getting" this stuff. But I "get" it and I love it.', '2008-03-07 10:54:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(4545949, 646750, 61651, '<td valign="top">Striking and enigmatic image, with an unassuming presentation.  I feel like there is a person to know in this portrait.  Nice take on the challenge theme.</td>', 'Striking and enigmatic image, with an unassuming presentation.  I feel like there is a person to know in this portrait.  Nice take on the challenge theme.', '2008-03-07 15:10:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(4546117, 648706, 45475, '<td valign="top">I see where you were going with this, and I gave you a 5 for the effort. However, you have a serious issue with focus and light here. Maybe next time choose an place with more light and perhaps have someone else take the photo for you over your shoulder? That would eliminate the camera shake that''s made this so blurry.</td>', 'I see where you were going with this, and I gave you a 5 for the effort. However, you have a serious issue with focus and light here. Maybe next time choose an place with more light and perhaps have someone else take the photo for you over your shoulder? That would eliminate the camera shake that''s made this so blurry.', '2008-03-07 15:55:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4550078, 648839, 85102, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mollyh:</b></div><hr/><i> Looks a little grainy, but beautiful nonetheless. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>hehe, its wicked hard to make sand look "un-grainy"</td>', 'Originally posted by mollyh: Looks a little grainy, but beautiful nonetheless.  hehe, its wicked hard to make sand look "un-grainy"', '2008-03-09 13:42:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(4567714, 648605, 90947, '<td valign="top">This is an absolutely wonderful white on white shot.  Had you planned on a white on white shot?  You <u>should </u>be very happy with how it turned out.  I agree with all your comments and those of the rest of the reviewers.<br/> <br/>I would have preferred seeing the bird flying into frame instead of out of frame, but that is a trivial difference.  In any event, it is head an shoulders above anything I ever produced.</td>', 'This is an absolutely wonderful white on white shot.  Had you planned on a white on white shot?  You should be very happy with how it turned out.  I agree with all your comments and those of the rest of the reviewers. I would have preferred seeing the bird flying into frame instead of out of frame, but that is a trivial difference.  In any event, it is head an shoulders above anything I ever produced.', '2008-03-16 15:48:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4586548, 648706, 32933, '<td valign="top"><img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=45475" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">rinac</a> is right, but I <i>love</i> the set up, even if the photo itself didn''t turn out amazing.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-03-25 19:07:31.</i></td>', ' rinac is right, but I love the set up, even if the photo itself didn''t turn out amazing.', '2008-03-25 19:06:42.000000', '2008-03-25 19:07:31.000000', 0),
